## The IGI Precision Standard

IGI — the International Gemological Institute — is the correct certification for any lab grown asscher cut diamond you buy. Understanding what it means and how to read it prevents Mistake 2 and saves you real money.

IGI issues lab-grown diamond certificates that include the same information as a GIA certificate: cut grade (where applicable), color, clarity, carat weight, dimensions, and proportion data. For asscher cut diamonds, IGI issues a cut quality assessment, depth and table percentages, and a polish and symmetry grade.

There are two versions of IGI lab certification. The older format includes basic grading. The newer IGI lab report (post-2022) follows stricter calibration protocols for lab-grown stones and includes proportion data that is especially important for step-cuts like asscher. Always confirm the certificate is a full IGI Lab-Grown Diamond Report, not just a basic identification report.

### IGI vs GIA for Lab Grown Asscher — Direct Comparison

| Factor | IGI Lab | GIA Lab | What this means |
|---|---|---|---|
| Price premium | Baseline | 10–20% higher | GIA lab cert costs more without adding visual quality |
| Lab specialization | Calibrated for lab | Natural standards applied | IGI grades lab specifically; more consistent for lab-to-lab comparisons |
| Accepted by insurers | Yes | Yes | Both work for insurance purposes — no practical difference |
| Accepted by retailers | Yes | Yes | Both are recognized at all major jewelry retailers |
| Secondary market | Slightly less | Slightly more | Only meaningful if selling privately to GIA-only buyers |
| Cut grade for asscher | Yes (IGI grades step-cuts) | Not issued for asscher | IGI is actually more informative on cut for asscher specifically |

**Verdict:** IGI for all lab grown asscher cut diamonds for personal use. GIA lab only has an edge on secondary market resale with private buyers — a niche scenario. For wearing the ring, IGI gives you the same quality assurance at a lower price and better cut information for step-cuts.

