## Expert Summary

A lab grown asscher cut diamond gives you access to the most demanding step-cut in fine jewelry at a price that makes D-IF the baseline, not the ceiling. The 4 mistakes in this post are the difference between a purchase you love and a purchase you regret.

Don't buy VS2 in a lab asscher — the step-cut shows it. Don't pay for GIA lab certification when IGI gives you the same quality stone for less. Don't compare lab to natural by price-per-carat — compare face-up size and total cost, and natural loses at every carat weight above 1ct. And don't downgrade color when D is $300 more.

The [asscher cut diamond pillar page](/asscher-cut-diamond) covers the full proportions guide, depth/table spec, and Art Deco history if you want to go deeper. The [loose asscher cut diamond guide](/loose-asscher-cut-diamond) covers the natural vs lab comparison from the natural buyer's perspective.

